{"title":"2011 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The sum of two angles of a triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/f/e4fc4c669518d5da6185c95ea46645895843844d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{6}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> of a right angle, and one of these two angles is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/3/e73393067e6d6e401a5354accc7a730c7a2977aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" /> larger than the other. What is the degree measure of the largest angle in the triangle?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/4/0847bac2d53dee206c23623c037c4edee9e09158.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 69 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 72 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 90 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 102 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 108$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"412\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The sum of two angles in a triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/f/e4fc4c669518d5da6185c95ea46645895843844d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{6}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> of a right angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/a/e6af7cf7ba0ba7ff8053357796cf8c67af5fd233.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\longrightarrow \\frac{6}{5} \\times 90 = 108$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"138\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is the measure of the first angle, then the measure of the second angle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/1/5313d44901ff7f466d3054cec2d1740241b5dca9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/b/18bf4d3e6772d54562d7ac37e5725731ac30c340.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x + x + 30 = 108 \\longrightarrow 2x = 78 \\longrightarrow x = 39\\]\" width=\"327\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Now we know the measure of two angles are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/c/61c1de7374c98f545caa2c4cb7633eeb627171a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$39^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/3/43376841be714bd279d36f178ddb35655497aa5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$69^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" />. By the Triangle Sum Theorem, the sum of all angles in a triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/b/5ab8f36b3d6a85590cc8b2629daa58e3559df11f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^{\\circ},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"39\" height=\"16\" /> so the final angle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/b/24b827998def193fbf2d8ec73227dc09a0a27e63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$72^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" />. Therefore, the largest angle in the triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/9/1e967ab0e1030c0d9bd25d6542660c11e0872580.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\mathrm{(B) \\ } 72}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"62\" height=\"29\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B\" title=\"2011 AMC 10B\">2011 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2011 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2011 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2011 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2011 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2011 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2011 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2011 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2011 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2011 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> 